  "explanation": {
    "short": "Latin is said as it is written, and every letter is said: the final e too, so vale is VAH-leh. The letter h is silent: hic sounds like \"eek\". The letter v is as in English, and a double letter, as in Anna, is held a little longer.",
    "more": "The five vowels are pure, as in Italian: a as in \"father\", e as in \"bed\", i as in \"machine\", o as in \"for\", u as in \"rule\". A word of two syllables, like AN-na, VAH-leh and IL-leh, is stressed on the first syllable."
  },
